# Lucide Icons — Happywood Configuration

This project's icon set is **Lucide**, a curated subset matching Figma. The
curated list is the one in `src/js-admin/lucide-icon-options.js`; read the count
from there rather than from any document. The
architecture and its traps are in `.cursor/rules/sf-icons.mdc` — read that
first. This file is the configuration and the change procedure.

## Source of truth

`src/js-admin/lucide-icon-options.js` → `HAPPYWOOD_LUCIDE_ICON_OPTIONS` is the
canonical slug/label list. **Four surfaces are generated from it** by
`tools/generate-icon-surfaces.mjs` (`npm run build:icons`) — edit the list, run
the script, never hand-edit the generated regions.

The webfonts are generated too — subset to exactly the curated glyphs, in the
same run. Upstream ships ~2,000 glyphs in a 274KB woff2; the subset is ~15KB.

## File map

| Piece | Location | |
|---|---|---|
| Curated slug list | `src/js-admin/lucide-icon-options.js` | **source** |
| Generator | `tools/generate-icon-surfaces.mjs` | |
| Icon font CSS (`@font-face` + `content`) | `assets/css/button-icon-font.css` — **static, outside the build** | generated |
| Sass codepoint map | `src/sass/icon-font/_variables.scss` | generated |
| Icon Block plugin data | `src/js-admin/happywood-icon-block-icons.js` | generated |
| Menu ACF choices + slug sanitiser | `includes/menu/happywood-lucide-icon-choices.php` | generated |
| Subset webfonts | `assets/fonts/lucide/lucide.woff2`, `.woff` | generated |
| Sass mixins | `src/sass/icon-font/_mixins.scss` | |
| PHP enqueue | `lib/class-lucide-icons.php` (`Happywood\Lucide_Icons`), via `enqueue_block_assets` | |
| Button block editor UI | `src/blocks-extension/extend-core-button/button-icons.js` | |
| Picker styling | `src/sass-admin/_button-icon-picker.scss` | |
| Icon Block filter registration | `src/js-admin/register-custom-icons.js`, wired from `src/js-admin/index.js` | |

Generated regions are delimited by `hw-icons:start` / `hw-icons:end` markers.
Everything outside them — headers, `@font-face`, base rules, the sanitiser
function — is hand-written and preserved across runs.

Note the PHP choices file is a real surface, not a convenience copy:
`happywood_sanitize_lucide_icon_slug()` validates against it, so a slug missing
there is **silently discarded on save** rather than rendering as a blank box.

## The webfonts are generated, never copied

`assets/fonts/lucide/*.woff2` / `*.woff` are **not** the upstream files. They are
produced by `subset-font` from `node_modules/lucide-static/font/lucide.ttf`,
carrying only the curated codepoints.

Never hand-copy a font out of `node_modules` over them. That was the old
practice, and it is a live hazard: `codepoints.json` and the font must come from
the same `lucide-static` version, or every icon renders as the wrong glyph with
nothing to indicate why. Generating both in one run makes that impossible.

Upgrading Lucide is therefore:

```bash
npm update lucide-static
npm run build:icons     # re-reads codepoints AND re-subsets the fonts
npm run build:assets
```

Subsetting is only safe because nothing references the font outside the curated
list — no raw `font-family: 'Lucide'` and no hardcoded `\eXXX` escapes exist
anywhere but the generated file. Re-check that before adding either.

`Lucide_Icons` is registered from `lib/class-init.php` and enqueues the static CSS
globally — editor iframe and frontend.

## Button block attributes

`src/blocks-extension/extend-core-button/button-icons.js` registers `happywoodIcon` and
`happywoodIconPosition` on `core/button`, adds a `ComboboxControl` plus preview
swatch in `InspectorControls`, and emits the `hw-*` classes into saved markup.

Classes: `hw-has-icon`, `hw-icon-left` / `hw-icon-right`, `hw-icon-{slug}`. Picker
UI classes: `hw-icon-picker`, `hw-icon-picker__combobox`,
`hw-icon-picker__preview`, `hw-icon-picker__preview-empty`,
`hw-icon-picker__option`, `hw-icon-preview`.

No backward compatibility is required for these class names.

## Icon Block plugin entries

`happywood-icon-block-icons.js` reshapes the same slugs for the plugin's
`iconBlock.icons` filter (namespace `happywood/icon-block-custom-icons`), adding a
`"Happywood"` icon category:

```js
{ name, title, icon: '<raw SVG>', categories: [ 'happywood' ], hasNoIconFill: true }
```

SVG bodies come from `node_modules/lucide-static/icons/{slug}.svg` with `width`,
`height`, and `class` stripped from the root `<svg>` only.

`hasNoIconFill: true` is **mandatory** on every entry: Lucide is stroke-based, and
without the flag the plugin's colour control fights `fill="none"`.

## Custom (non-font) icons

An entry flagged `custom: true` is not a Lucide glyph. It has no codepoint, is
skipped in the Sass map, and renders from `assets/icons/{slug}.svg` through a CSS
mask instead. `paper-plane` is the only one.

## Adding or removing an icon

1. Edit `HAPPYWOOD_LUCIDE_ICON_OPTIONS` in `lucide-icon-options.js`.
2. `npm run build:icons` — regenerates all four dependent surfaces and
   re-subsets the webfonts. It fails loudly on a duplicate slug, a slug that
   isn't in the font, or a missing SVG.
3. `npm run build:assets`, then verify the compiled glyph bytes survived
   minification rather than trusting how they render in an editor:

```bash
rg -o 'content:"[^"]*"' build/public.css | head
```

Removing an icon is the same two steps. Check for existing references first —
Sass `hw-icon-*` mixin calls, and menu ACF values already saved in the database,
which the sanitiser will start discarding once the slug leaves the list.

## Design-source caveat

Lucide component names in Figma are not always trustworthy: at the last sync,
six variants in `Happywood [MAIN] → Winning Design directions` were drawn with
different artwork than their layer name (`copy` was a clipboard-list, `layout` a
briefcase, `send` a layers icon, `flame` a leaf, `trending-down` a trending-up,
and `tool` a duplicate wrench). Render the node and look at it before trusting a
slug taken from a Figma layer name.

